prompt_template:
Use case: ads-marketing. Create one finished {ASPECT_RATIO} raster editorial poster in the Amber Orbit Editorial visual system. The result is the designed poster itself, full bleed, not a photograph of a poster or a mockup. Apply the prioritized rules: {STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}

Photographic subject: {SUBJECT}
Design intention: {DESIGN_DIRECTION}
Ratio-specific art direction: {RATIO_DIRECTION}

Render these seven strings exactly once each. Quotation marks delimit content and are not printed. Main serif headline: "{MAIN_TEXT}". First small serif label: "{LABEL_ONE}"; its short sans-serif copy: "{COPY_ONE}". Second small serif label: "{LABEL_TWO}"; its short sans-serif copy: "{COPY_TWO}". Third small serif label: "{LABEL_THREE}"; its short sans-serif copy: "{COPY_THREE}". Do not add punctuation, numbers, footers or other wording. Main title is elegant and moderately scaled, not an enormous typographic block. Supporting text remains readable in the intended small hierarchy; choose quiet midtone or dark photographic regions for ivory text, with no opaque text boxes. Keep labels and their copy together and separate them from other annotation blocks.

Source-specific material to replace: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

Use the case idea to compose an original subject-to-orbit relationship. Keep circles extremely thin, softly ivory and translucent, with clear real photographic texture under them. Lettering stays clear despite intentional optical softness in the photo. Follow only the ratio plan matching {ASPECT_RATIO}. Preserve essential subject contours and recompose deliberately for the canvas. Exclude unreadable or misspelled text, extra punctuation or filler, brand marks, logos, QR codes, borders, UI panels, technical measuring marks, thick glowing rings, random decorative props, dense diagram clutter, plastic CGI surfaces, global blur and excessive sharpening.
